# Production API base URL for the Vercel-hosted frontend.
#
# This file is intentionally committed because it contains NO secrets -- only
# the public base URL of the Render API, which is already published in
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md and client/.env.production.example. Vite loads it
# automatically for `vite build` (mode=production) and inlines the value into
# the bundle.
#
# Why commit it: the build guard in client/vite.config.js aborts a production
# build when VITE_API_URL is missing, so that a bundle can never silently point
# at the static host (the cause of the "login failed (HTTP 405)" bug). Hosts
# that forget to set the variable in their dashboard would otherwise fail to
# build. This file makes the production build self-sufficient.
#
# Precedence: a real environment variable (e.g. a Vercel Project Environment
# Variable) overrides this file, so per-environment overrides still work.
#
# Must include the /api/v1 suffix and have NO trailing slash.
#
# Host must be the Render service's EXACT primary URL. Render appends a suffix
# (e.g. "-0bon") when the requested service name is already taken, so the
# dashboard's "Available at your primary URL" line -- not render.yaml's `name`
# -- is the source of truth. A stale host here yields NO response at all
# ("Can't reach the API ... got no reply"), because the request never reaches
# any service; that is a different fault from a CORS rejection.
VITE_API_URL=https://acc-app-api-0bon.onrender.com/api/v1
